tors: From Understanding to Application quantity Enroll Now Overview Learn AI for media in a 100% online, self-paced course from Poynter. Finish in 4–5 hours, or dive deeper with 8–10 hours of optional content. Explore 4 modules: AI landscape, tools, assessment, misinformation, ethics. Gain practical skills to streamline research, draft smarter and work faster. Learn to spot AI risks like bias, errors and misinformation before they spread. Apply AI transparently to protect your credibility and audience trust. Earn a Poynter Certificate — recognized worldwide in journalism and media. Enroll anytime, learn anywhere — this course is fully self-directed online. Training 5 or More People? get consulting & coaching Description Schedule Requirements AI for Journalists and Content Creators: From Understanding to Application The definitive course for journalists, creators and media professionals navigating the AI age. Artificial intelligence is rewriting the rules of media. Journalists, creators and media professionals are under pressure to move faster and do more — without sacrificing accuracy, credibility or trust. Most AI courses stop at prompting tricks. This Poynter-developed program goes deeper, focusing on strategy, impact and ethics. You’ll learn how to streamline research, generate smarter drafts and test ideas quickly, while also gaining the skills to spot AI risks like bias, misinformation and hallucinations before they harm your work. Just as importantly, you’ll practice applying AI transparently and ethically so your audience knows they can trust your process. The course is 100% self-directed and takes about four to five hours to complete, with optional deeper content. Through four modules you’ll explore how AI is changing journalism, practice refining prompts for better results, compare platforms for speed and accuracy, and examine real examples of deepfakes and misinformation. Along the way, you’ll apply journalism ethics to AI dilemmas and review newsroom policies you can adapt to your own work. Completing the program earns you a Poynter certificate, recognized as a mark of excellence in journalism and media training, and positions you as the AI voice in your newsroom or creator community — able to evaluate tools, benchmark outputs and shape responsible policy. Meet a Poynter AI Expert: Alex Mahadevan Alex Mahadevan, Poynter’s Director of MediaWise and a faculty member who is a leading voice on AI, brings deep experience training both professional journalists and digital creators worldwide. He is trusted by major newsrooms and platforms for his ability to make complex technology accessible, ethical and actionable. “AI is not about replacing journalists or creators — it’s about strengthening our ability to tell the truth faster, with more depth and more trust. This course is designed to give you the confidence and skills to lead the way.” — Alex Mahadevan Why Poynter? No other organization sits at the intersection of journalism, media, ethics and real-world practice like The Poynter Institute. We train media leaders across the globe. Our faculty live and work in journalism’s unique realities, from breaking news to investigative reporting to creator-driven platforms. With Poynter, you’re not just learning tools. You’re preparing for the future of media. What Participants Are Saying “I like the substantive, non-hyperbolic way you approach AI tools and trends and how to apply them thoughtfully in journalism.” — Participant, pilot program NEW : This course is eligible for Professional Development Units (PDUs) through the Project Management Institute’s Authorized Training Partner program and may be applied toward maintaining PMI credentials. Participants earn 5 Professional Development Units recognized by the Project Management Institute — 1.5 in Ways of Working, 1.5 in Power Skills and 2 in Business Acumen. Poynter’s authorized PMI partnership lets you earn credits while building critical skills. Questions? If you need assistance, email us at info@poynter.org . This is a 100% self-directed, online course you can begin anytime. Most learners complete the program in four to five hours, though optional deep-dive activities and exercises extend the experience to eight to 10 hours. You will have full access to all materials, so you can pause, revisit lessons and learn at your own pace. Here’s how the course breaks down: Module 1: The landscape of AI in journalism and media (30–45 minutes) Understand the current state of AI, how it is shaping media, and what it means for credibility and public trust. Includes a short quiz and reflection exercise. Module 2: Practical applications for AI tools (45 minutes) Explore leading tools such as ChatGPT, Claude and NotebookLM. Learn effective prompting techniques and practice fixing prompts to get better results. Module 3: Choosing and assessing AI tools (2 to 2.5 hours) Learn criteria for tool selection, compare platforms, and complete interactive exercises benchmarking speed, accuracy and bias. Includes a scenario-based tool selection activity. Module 4: Ethics and standards of generative AI (1.5 to 2 hours) Apply core journalism ethics to AI use and the verification of AI-generated content, review examples of newsroom policies and work through ethical dilemmas. Ends with a capstone reflection on how you will apply AI responsibly in your role. At the end of each module, you will complete practical exercises, knowledge checks and reflection prompts designed to apply what you have learned immediately to your newsroom, organization or creative practice. Upon finishing all four modules, you will receive a Poynter certificate of completion — proof of your expertise in ethical, practical AI for media. Who should enroll? This webinar is essential for reporters, editors, newsroom leaders and anyone involved in news gathering and publishing who wants to understand the legal landscape and reinforce best practices for protecting their work. Cost $95. Questions? 