      "evidenceText": "MediaWise - Poynter MediaWise - Poynter DONATE What do you want to search? Submit Sign In | Membership News Training Ethics Fact-Checking Media Literacy AI Events Future of Public Media Newmark Ethics Center IFCN MediaWise PolitiFact Donate About Us Press Freedom Watch The Poynter 50 Podcasts Artificial Intelligence Business & Work Reporting & Editing Fact-Checking Ethics & Trust Local News Journalism, Media & Communication Training Poynter Membership Categories Consulting & Coaching For ACES Members For Local News Funders All Categories Broadcast & Visual Journalism Business & Work Ethics Fact-Checking & Media Literacy Leadership Reporting & Editing Writing Poynter ACES Introductory Certificate in Editing Poynter ACES Intermediate Certificate in Editing Poynter ACES Advanced Certificate in Editing Workshops and Coaching Tools for Funders Ethics Ethics Training Ethics Articles AI Ethics Public Editor Project Get Ethics Advice Fact-Checking Articles IFCN IFCN Grants International Fact-Checking Day Teen Creator Network PolitiFact MediaWise Media Literacy Resources AI Literacy Ambassadors Teen Creator Network Research & News International en Español MediaWise Training All Events The 2026 Poynter Journalism Prizes Empowering a media literate world MediaWise strengthens communities around the world with practical media and AI literacy skills that address the information challenges they face in their daily lives. By making media literacy accessible and practical through innovative design, MediaWise empowers communities to make informed decisions and participate confidently in a rapidly changing digital world. Get started with resources for Who is MediaWise? MediaWise launched in 2018 with a goal of empowering 1 million Gen Zers across the U.S. with the skills they need to find trusted sources and make sense of the vast amount of information at their fingertips. We met that goal within one year. Since then, MediaWise has broadened its reach to engage with and create resources for learners of all ages, re aching over 151 million people globally. Through international partnerships, MediaWise works across 30 countries. With simple yet effective media and AI literacy skills, we aim to meet people where they are and walk with them through every step to determine what’s real and what’s not on the internet. Through MediaWise, everyone can do their part to reduce the spread of misinformation and elevate the facts. Explore our work Find our media and information literacy curriculum and resources Media Literacy Level up your AI understanding with curriculum and training AI Literacy See how we amplify media literacy through trusted voices Ambassador Program Learn about our youth-centered work Teen Creator Network Dive deeper into research and news coverage about our work See Mediawise in Action MediaWise works all over the world International Encuentre nuestros recursos de alfabetización mediática en español En Español Get started with online learning led by MediaWise experts Classes and Training MediaWise Team Alex Mahadevan MediaWise Director and Poynter Faculty Alex Mahadevan is faculty at Poynter and director of MediaWise, Poynter’s digital media literacy project that teaches people of all ages how to spot misinformation... Read More Brittani Kollar Deputy Director, MediaWise Brittani Kollar is the deputy director of MediaWise, Poynter’s digital media literacy project. In this role, she oversees MediaWise’s global strategic partnerships, programming and operations,... Read More Sean Marcus Interactive Learning Designer, MediaWise As the Interactive Learning Designer for MediaWise, Sean Marcus designs and develops learning material for a wide range of audiences and purposes, ranging from senior... Read More Jessi Hollis McCarthy Program Specialist, MediaWise Jessi Hollis McCarthy is the program specialist of MediaWise, Poynter’s digital media literacy project that teaches people of all ages how to spot misinformation o